{"id":"u-d200f5d1-b80f-40fb-ac78-e28c8e397705","src":"community","title":"Lift, Grow, Empower: Glute Builder","author":"Josh O.","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/8fMwqY-abbeys-hammies","desc":"This 4-day full-body program is designed for women who want to build size and strength in their hamstrings and glutes, while toning their quads and keeping an athletic, lean physique.\n\nEach workout is thoughtfully designed with simple structure, defined goals, and clear instructions so you can build strength and sculpt your lower body with confidence.\n\n⸻\n\nWhat You’ll Do Each Week:\n\t•\tDay 1 – Lower Body: Glute & Hamstring Strength + Core\n\t•\tDay 2 – Upper Body (Push & Pull) + Glute Burnout\n\t•\tDay 3 – Lower Body: Quads + Glutes + Core\n\t•\tDay 4 – Full Body Strength + Explosive Finisher\n\n⸻\n\nKey Concepts & Definitions:\n\t•\tProgressive Overload:\nThe most important principle in strength training. It means gradually increasing the weight, reps, or sets you do over time so your muscles stay challenged and continue growing stronger. For example, if you did 3 sets of 8 reps at 50 lbs last week, try 55 lbs this week—or 9 reps instead of 8.\n\n\t•\tCompound Exercises:\nThese work multiple muscle groups at once, such as squats, deadlifts, hip thrusts, and lunges. They build strength efficiently and are the core of this program.\n\n\t•\tAccessory (or Isolation) Exercises:\nThese target specific muscles, like leg curls for hamstrings or leg extensions for quads. You’ll use these to sculpt and tone.\n\n\t•\tReps (Repetitions):\nOne complete movement of an exercise. For example, lifting and lowering a dumbbell in a bicep curl = 1 rep.\n\n\t•\tSets:\nA group of repetitions. For example, 3 sets of 10 reps means you’ll do 10 reps, rest, and repeat that 3 times.\n\n\t•\tRIR (Reps in Reserve):\nHow many more reps you could do at the end of a set. If you stop a set with 2 RIR, you could’ve done 2 more reps with good form. This helps prevent injury while still training hard.\n\n\t•\tGlute Finisher:\nA quick, high-rep burnout at the end of a workout to really target and fatigue your glutes for maximum growth.\n\n\t•\tDeload Week:\nA lighter week every 4–6 weeks to give your body time to recover and come back stronger. Use less weight, fewer sets, or skip intense finishers.\n\n⸻\n\nBuilt-In Progression Plan:\n\t•\tWeeks 1–2: Learn proper form, focus on control.\n\t•\tWeeks 3–4: Increase weights, reps, or add a set to each exercise.\n\t•\tWeek 5: Deload (lighter volume or effort).\n\t•\tWeek 6+: Start over with higher baselines and build again!\n\n\n\nNutrition Reminders\n\t•\tEat slightly above maintenance for muscle building\n\t•\tProtein target: ~1g per lb of bodyweight (~100-110g/day)\n\t•\tFocus on nutrient-dense carbs for recovery: oats, rice, sweet potatoes","level":["Intermediate"],"goals":["Athletics","Women's","Muscle"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":70,"joins":5,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-07-07T18:55:04.665Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Lower Body (Glute & Hamstring)","Upper Body + Glute Burnout","Lower Body + Core","Full Body Strength + Plyo"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Hip Thrust (Barbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":7,"x":4}]},{"n":"Romanian Deadlift (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":7,"x":4}]},{"n":"Bulgarian Split Squat (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":7,"x":3}],"note":"8 reps each leg"},{"n":"Lying Leg Curl","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":9,"x":3}],"note":"Use seated leg curl if preferred"},{"n":"Glute Kickback (Cable)","sets":[{"r":15,"rpe":7,"x":3}],"note":"15 reps each leg. \n\nAlt: Glute drive machine"},{"n":"Hanging Leg Raise","sets":[{"r":15,"rpe":10,"x":3}],"note":"Alt: Hanging leg raise or ab wheel"}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":8,"rpe":7,"x":4}]},{"n":"Lat Pulldown (Neutral Grip)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":7,"x":4}]},{"n":"Lateral Raise (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"r":12,"rpe":8,"x":3}]},{"n":"Seated Row (Cable)","sets":[{"r":10,"rpe":7,"x":3}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Bicep Curl (Cable)","s